WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.540
At home, Piotr shows Anna some photos of his family.

2
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.750
Kto to jest?

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.320
To jest moja siostra, Ola.

4
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:11.890
A to?

5
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.620
To jest mój brat, Tomek.

6
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:20.730
The word for my changed. It follows the gender of the person.

7
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.100
A ty? Masz rodzeństwo?

8
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.510
Tak, mam siostrę.

9
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.740
To jest mój tata.

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:35.140
The word for my agrees with the person you present.

11
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.170
One form goes with women, another with men.

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.760
And after the verb to have, a feminine word changes its last letter.

13
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.880
Present your mum. This is my mum.

14
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.900
To jest moja mama.

15
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.460
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

16
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.780
To jest moja mama.

17
00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:08.620
You have a sister. Say it.

18
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.320
Mam siostrę.

19
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.880
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

20
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.880
Mam siostrę.

21
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.080
Ask a friend if they have brothers or sisters.

22
00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:30.980
Masz rodzeństwo?

23
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.540
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

24
00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.740
Masz rodzeństwo?

25
00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.380
Now practise with the exercises below the video.
